 "title": "Не мой паштет  (Not My Pâté)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Barinov has taken a spoonful of Max's pâté. Max is waiting for the compliment, and what he gets is not quite what he hoped for. First the Russian.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Неплохо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Только это не мой паштет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Как?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Та же консистенция.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "И состав я подобрал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что входит в ваш паштет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это секрет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Пойдём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотрим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back through it a line at a time.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Неплохо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Not bad.' It's one word, with the 'ne' stuck to the front of 'bad'. From Barinov, this counts as very high praise.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Huh?' It's just 'yes?' with a rising voice, and means 'really?'. Max is fishing for more.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Только это не мой паштет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Only this isn't my pâté.' The first word can mean 'only' or 'but', and here it means 'but'. The 'not' is in front of 'my'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Как?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What?' Max says 'how?', which is what Russians say when they are stunned. It is just one word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Та же консистенция.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The same texture.' 'The same' is a pair of tiny words, with the 'a' ending to match the feminine noun. 'Texture' is a borrowed word, and a long one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "И состав я подобрал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And I got the ingredients right.' The word for 'composition' stands for ingredients, as in what a thing consists of. Max puts it first, which gives it extra weight.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait.' This is the polite command, with the 'ite' ending. Max is speaking to his boss, so he stays polite.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что входит в ваш паштет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What goes into your pâté?' The ingredients 'enter' it, which is how Russians ask what's inside. 'Your' is the polite masculine form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это секрет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's a secret.' There's no 'is' and no 'a'. It's just 'this secret', and Barinov keeps it short.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Пойдём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's go.' The 'we' form of the word for 'go' doubles as 'let's go'. It's a quick, casual invitation.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотрим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's have a look.' This is the 'we' form again, now of 'look', so it means 'we'll see' too. Barinov can't resist a dramatic pause.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Okay.' It's a single word, and Max says it quietly. He doesn't yet know what he'll find. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Неплохо.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Только это не мой паштет.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Как?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Та же консистенция.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "И состав я подобрал.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что входит в ваш паштет?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это секрет.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Пойдём.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотрим.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max thought he had won, and now he is not sure what he's missed. The way Barinov says 'not bad' is as high as his praise goes, so enjoy it. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "До свидания!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
